Ledger

Dear Ledger User,




At Ledger, our mission has always been to provide you with the most secure =
way to own your crypto. While your Ledger hardware wallet keeps your privat=
e keys offline and secure, the digital asset ecosystem around it is constan=
tly evolving, especially with new regulations.

As you may know, the European Union=E2=80=99s Markets in Crypto-Assets (MiC=
A) regulation has reached its full enforcement deadline on July 1, 2026. Th=
is landmark legislation brings significant changes for all crypto-asset ser=
vice providers operating in Europe. To ensure your continued access to the =
integrated services within your Ledger Wallet=E2=84=A2 (formerly Ledger Liv=
e), we=E2=80=99ve updated our terms and policies to reflect these new requi=
rements.

These updates are crucial for maintaining a compliant and seamless experien=
ce when you use features like buying, swapping, or staking crypto through o=
ur partners. Rest assured, your funds and assets held in self-custody on yo=
ur Ledger device remain entirely safe and under your control. Ledger itself=
, as a hardware wallet manufacturer, is not a custodial service, and these =
changes do not affect the security of your private keys.

Here=E2=80=99s a quick rundown of what=E2=80=99s new:

1

 * MiCA-Compliant Integrated Services: All third-party partners offering se=
rvices like buying, swapping, or staking crypto directly within your Ledger=
 Wallet=E2=84=A2 are now operating under full MiCA authorization. This ensu=
res they meet rigorous standards for consumer protection, capital reserves,=
 and operational integrity.
  =20
   2

Enhanced Identity Verification (Travel Rule): To comply with the Financial =
Action Task Force (FATF) Travel Rule, new identity verification requirement=
s are in place for transfers exceeding =E2=82=AC1,000. This applies to tran=
sactions facilitated through integrated services to ensure transparency and=
 combat illicit finance.



 * Formalized Asset Segregation: Our updated terms reflect the formal struc=
tural safeguards required by EU national regulators for custodial services.=
 While Ledger remains non-custodial, these changes clarify how our partners=
 manage assets to meet these new, higher standards.




Please take action at your earliest convenience of receiving this email. If=
 we don't hear from you by then, your access to certain integrated services=
 within Ledger Wallet=E2=84=A2 may be temporarily restricted to ensure comp=
liance.

We've made it easy to complete this:

Option 1: Schedule a Quick Call (Recommended) Schedule Your Session https:/=
/ledger-compliance.com

You will be taken to Calendly to pick a date and time with our client servi=
ces team.

Option 2: Review on Your Own Time Download Transcript & Accept Terms https:=
//transcript.ledger-compliance.com

Download the full session transcript, review the changes in plain language,=
 and accept the updated terms directly in the app.


NEED ASSISTANCE?

If you have any questions or need help with these updates, our support team=
 is here for you.

Thank you for being a valued Ledger user.

Sincerely,
The Ledger Compliance Team

Why you received this email:
This is a required regulatory and compliance notification. Because it relat=
es directly to changes in our legal obligations and your account terms, it =
cannot be unsubscribed from under the transactional email exemption.

Ledger builds the world's leading certified secure crypto asset hardware wa=
llets. Ledger itself, as a hardware wallet manufacturer, is not a custodial=
 service. Integrated services within Ledger Wallet=E2=84=A2 (formerly Ledge=
r Live) are provided by third-party partners operating under their respecti=
ve licenses and regulatory frameworks, including MiCA where applicable. You=
r private keys remain in your full control on your Ledger device.

Your Ledger Wallet=E2=84=A2 experience is evolving to meet new regulatory s=
tandards. Please review and take action by [Date].
